# vehje-runtime-abi. Design

The framework's per-script wire family: what crosses the compiler-to-runtime
boundary and in what representation. Pure type surface plus the `extern "C"`
entry, no runtime logic. `#![no_std]`, no alloc. Bare primitives appear only at
the `#[repr(C)]` wire boundary, the one documented FFI exception, not in the
crate's own logic.

One crate, not two, even though it carries a residual arena and a value-arena:
they are one structural family (the value-arena reuses the residual arena's
child-index-and-blob layout) and the record layout must have exactly one
definition. Internally it splits into four modules, `wire`, `value`, `sink`, and
`entry`, drawn so that if the value side outgrows the file-size smell it splits
as files under one crate, never a second crate with a copied layout.

## The residual (the wire module)

The residual is a control-flow-graph-of-blocks program, not a flat value. The
runtime parses, lowers, and executes it for arriving scripts, so the wire form
models a program, and this is where the debt that the runtime contains a compile
stage lands.

- `Residual`. The crossing descriptor: the serialized node arena, the child-index
  pool, the string blob, the block table, the function table, and the root. The
  node records carry inline operands (pool indirection is the measured expensive
  part, so operands stay inline; the exact inline count is a measure-then-lock
  constant with a provisional value, the earlier 24-byte-three-operand figure
  having washed to a null result at scale).
- The block and function tables. A block is a maximal straight-line region (a
  contiguous node range with backward-only child indices); the block table
  records each block's node range, terminator kind, successor block ids, and
  block-argument signature, and the function table records each function's entry
  block and argument and result signatures. Control flow lives only at
  terminators; a loop is a back-edge with block-argument-passed loop-carried
  values, and a call saves a return record on a frame stack bounded by the depth
  cap. State: the block and function tables are the designed residual shape; the
  lowering that constructs them from `Node` is owed (it is downstream of `Anf`,
  which names the join points that give a nested branch its successor blocks),
  so the tables are the target the producer builds toward, not yet populated.
- `Tier`. Narrowed to name only the internal execution form (interpret the arena
  versus run the bytecode), not a native-versus-managed axis. Native is a
  method-agnostic point on the output spectrum, chosen where a per-region grade
  proves it wins, not a tier tag here.
- The diagnostics schema. The six additions that let the single engine
  reconstruct a lease or effect error's witness lazily on the failure path: the
  span table, the binder-site table, the per-relation provenance arrays, the
  violation seeds, an optional residual debug section, and the
  provenance-complete engine boundary. Landed in the wire format now so the
  reconstruction query has them.

## The value-arena (the value module)

The produced value crosses back as a value-arena: fixed-width value-node records,
a flat child-index pool, a self-contained byte blob, and relative index links,
the same structural family as the residual. It is region-structured: each value
node carries a region id through a region-table indirection (the table finalises
at chunk close, so no byte is touched twice and there is no back-patch), and
region open and close markers let the runtime free a region's segment on stack
discipline with no collector and no refcount.

- `ValueArena`. The value-arena format and its region table. Its records carry a
  declared `#[repr(C)]` layout (see the value-transport deep dive), the stable
  layout the zero-copy read depends on. `get` reads a node by index on the
  trusted path (valid only after validation); `try_get` returns `Maybe<ValueNode>`
  for the untrusted path, and the child accessor is clamped to the live pool, so a
  malformed arena is a `Maybe`/empty slice, not a panic.
- `ValueNode`. One value-node record, `#[repr(C)]`, fixed width.
- The backing memory is host-lent up front; the runtime holds no output memory
  after a call.

## The sink (the sink module)

- `VehjeSink`. The reserve-then-commit two-function transfer contract, one
  protocol for both boundaries: in-process a `#[repr(C)]` struct of two function
  pointers plus opaque userdata, out-of-process the executable's stdout pipe
  (the OS pipe buffer is the backpressure). The value serialises depth-first,
  children-before-parents, so a parent records already-known child indices with
  no back-patching, and streaming happens at whole-subtree chunk boundaries under
  a residency budget.

## The entry (the entry module)

- The one runtime-W batched-column `extern "C"` entry. It takes a column of W
  records per call (W at least two), so the runtime vectorises across the column,
  which is where the measured throughput lives. The crossing itself is nearly
  free, so there is no per-W symbol zoo and no crossing-amortisation cleverness
  beyond the column entry. The return contract is a value property: fallibility
  is an `Outcome`-shaped value in the value-arena, batch completion is a stream
  property on the sink, and the lane mask is an internal mask-and-continue
  mechanism, not a separate status vector.
- An `abi_version` on the public boundary.

## Non-scope

- Runtime execution (the Zig runtime).
- Compiler-side dispatch (`vehje-runtime-driver`).
- The validated-data package and manifest (`vehje-runtime-gen`).

## Dependencies

`vehje-ir` for the residual node layout the wire form mirrors; `arvo` for the
newtype discipline outside the FFI boundary; `hilavitkutin-str` for the string
blob identity. `#![no_std]`, no alloc.
